      en: "Mamoré River is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Bolivia. The Mamoré River is a large river in the Bolivian Amazon basin and one of the main tributaries of the Madeira River. Flows through northern Bolivia. Important transportation route. Joins the Beni River. This natural area reflects the scenic diversity of Bolivia, between the Andean Cordillera, the Altiplano, Lake Titicaca, the Salar de Uyuni, and the Amazon basin. Like many notable places in Bolivia, it combines regional character between the high Andes, the Altiplano, and the eastern Amazonian lowlands with wider significance. Thus, this place contributes to Bolivia's diverse profile, from Lake Titicaca and the Salar de Uyuni to the Yungas and the Amazon basin."
